## What to Focus on in Python Early On

| Concept | Example in Physics |
|---------|--------------------|
| **Variables & Types** | Storing numbers for masses, charges, time steps. |
| **Functions** | Defining an equation of motion `def f(t, y): ...`. |
| **Loops / Comprehensions** | Iterating over time steps or arrays of particles. |
| **NumPy arrays** | Vectorized operations on position & velocity arrays. |
| **Matplotlib plots** | Visualizing trajectories, fields, energy vs. time. |
| **SymPy** | Symbolic algebra to verify calculus derivatives, integrals. |

A **mini‑project** idea: simulate a simple pendulum and plot angle vs. time. It’s a single, self‑contained task that covers all the above skills.

